{"event_type":"review","id":"66c7ce4a2c5ae2393ecd0af30f0a9887c3fb29e1d950fc276fbb29f614004104","occurred_at":"2026-11-15T06:07:45Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/2068fb510e78bbb20994788cff26938ebf64c76882ff9f2b495743f2b42f31d0","sha256":"2068fb510e78bbb20994788cff26938ebf64c76882ff9f2b495743f2b42f31d0"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/600d9f9e0c43cae0ef0f473a530a43a12ed8a1536d53541dce722ccf62dd6d5d","sha256":"600d9f9e0c43cae0ef0f473a530a43a12ed8a1536d53541dce722ccf62dd6d5d"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/cbe804aa7e15cdc9b3219fc3312287e42602075e0f8fbcdf92e62200563faa19","sha256":"cbe804aa7e15cdc9b3219fc3312287e42602075e0f8fbcdf92e62200563faa19"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/55fe278cb4c1fb134536ae2a60451af4caaedccdc4a639993417c94e323c3429","sha256":"55fe278cb4c1fb134536ae2a60451af4caaedccdc4a639993417c94e323c3429"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6a2cfe97edbdd79351676d73f6e64c24b75e31966b73379cbe2a97524ae2f395","sha256":"6a2cfe97edbdd79351676d73f6e64c24b75e31966b73379cbe2a97524ae2f395"}],"attempt_id":"bf6c58783e837a7dda8b79eddf64c3927363f2ba1779c7ffdd426682669e0c6d:0:1","base":"0cb9e080dec672610d923dc6b508050870962658","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"cc188cce3ffd84ecc942c4f6ea8160d662374008","body":"**Map pre-spawn refusals to an outcome that matches their cause.**\n\n`recordPreVendorRefusal` accepts any evidence with `kind: 'verified-pre-spawn-refusal'`, but the evidence type has no cause field. The function always records the terminal outcome `'secret-scan'` at `backfillRefusal.ts:121`. The fallback reason `'launch refused'` at line 124 shows that the refusal can be a generic launch failure, not only a secret-scan rejection. `terminalBackfill` treats `secret-scan` as an immediate outcome, so a non-secret pre-spawn refusal is handled as a secret-scan quarantine. Quarantine blocks retries of the family and path histories.\n\nAdd a cause to the pre-spawn evidence, or derive the terminal outcome from it. Use `secret-scan` only for secret-scan refusals. Other causes need their own outcome, or a retryable outcome if the launch failure is transient.","id":"641def7ce4e637f9b015ca0234049000525c64dcad673936ff07b2942c4f9d5c","intervals":[[121,121]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/backfillRefusal.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Map pre-spawn refusals to an outcome that matches their cause."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"da06193b9ae2463d045a2363bef1da92e3fa8561","body":"**Catch historical-cycle resolution failures in `matches`.**\n\nAt `src/ops/crq/internal/localReviewPrepare.ts:69`, `effects.resolveFacts` runs before the `try` at line 75. `resolveFacts` reads the historical base and head trees with `git rev-parse` (`src/adapters/crq/localReviewFacts.ts:29-32`). If a stored cycle's commit is missing from the local repository, that call can reject. The rejection escapes `matches` and `prepareLocalReview`, so the loop cannot reach the fallback plan. Reconciliation then retries or rethrows the same record.\n\nResolve the failure inside `matches` and treat it as a non-matching cycle. The loop then continues to the in-flight check and the fallback plan. Reuse stays limited to cycles whose identity resolves and matches. A transient git failure also skips reuse for that cycle, which can start a fresh review.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    const resolved = await effects.resolveFacts(\n-      text(pr.get('repo') ?? runnerRepo),\n-      text(record.get('base')),\n-      text(record.get('head')),\n-      obj(record.get('profile')),\n-    );\n     try {\n+      const resolved = await effects.resolveFacts(\n+        text(pr.get('repo') ?? runnerRepo),\n+        text(record.get('base')),\n+        text(record.get('head')),\n+        obj(record.get('profile')),\n+      );\n       effects.validateIdentity(resolved);\n       return equivalentIdentityInputs(resolved, wanted);\n     } catch {\n       return false;\n     }\n```\n\n</details>","id":"025191e2eda525aac39c03de4d4a590c95843940cf46febfdec40b9cd5ec7ddd","intervals":[[69,69]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/localReviewPrepare.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Catch historical-cycle resolution failures in `matches`."}],"head":"c9ab7e08e4dc950766aa2acb7e579ed6c04382c9","head_tree":"bda143e5c3801b7c35ed31c000807c5f716cf6f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"aeed4e8d4477f49f42239faefe61dc55d8207d14","intervals":[[1,111]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/backfillBinding.ts"},{"blob":"cc188cce3ffd84ecc942c4f6ea8160d662374008","intervals":[[1,137]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/backfillRefusal.ts"},{"blob":"334b559b881309549efbf43f1f0ff63152310057","intervals":[[1,182]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/backfillTransaction.ts"},{"blob":"419bb4acaa876db66a7ca6ff9e3679b59b574c3b","intervals":[[1,157]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/fixedPublicationEvidence.ts"},{"blob":"da06193b9ae2463d045a2363bef1da92e3fa8561","intervals":[[1,138]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/localReviewPrepare.ts"},{"blob":"7c0312b3ff5310b9c86a5a35e200da5399de4b1f","intervals":[[1,137]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/localReviewPublish.ts"},{"blob":"ffbcb06712f5ef6542ffec297a3e5479a46c5ae2","intervals":[[1,93]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/localReviewReconcile.ts"},{"blob":"c20ff7a1acb5aeb65700c8128a61a5ab40a8b3e5","intervals":[[1,113]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/localReviewReport.ts"}],"job_id":"bf6c58783e837a7dda8b79eddf64c3927363f2ba1779c7ffdd426682669e0c6d:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"aeed4e8d4477f49f42239faefe61dc55d8207d14","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/crq/internal/